language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Cut raw rolls of a given width into pieces of several widths, using cutting patterns; each width must be cut at least as many times as its order requires, and the total number of raw rolls cut is minimised.
given roll_width : int(1..)
given widths_dim1 : int(1..)
given widths : matrix indexed by [int(1..widths_dim1)] of int(1..)
given orders : matrix indexed by [int(1..widths_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ num_rolls_width[p,j] is the number of pieces of width j that pattern p cuts from one roll
given num_rolls_width_dim1, num_rolls_width_dim2 : int(1..)
given num_rolls_width : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_rolls_width_dim1), int(1..num_rolls_width_dim2)] of int(0..)
$ patterns_used[p] is the number of rolls cut with pattern p
find patterns_used : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_rolls_width_dim1)] of int(0..sum(orders))
find min_rolls_cut : int(0..sum(orders))

minimising min_rolls_cut
such that
$ the total number of raw rolls cut is the sum of the rolls cut with each pattern
min_rolls_cut = (sum p : int(1..num_rolls_width_dim1) . patterns_used[p]),
$ for each width, the pieces cut over all patterns meet the order for that width
forAll j : int(1..widths_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..num_rolls_width_dim1) . patterns_used[p] * num_rolls_width[p,j]) >= orders[j]
